# Continuum API — Migration Test Requests
# Run the API first: bun run dev (port 3004)
#
# Migration identity is established ON-CHAIN: the real owner calls
# register_migration(old_collection, commitment) on the old rollup (owner = msg_sender, unforgeable).
# Continuum stores no wallet ↔ key mapping — it only mints secrets and resolves
# commitments → owners from indexed MigrationRegistered events.
#
# Variables — fill in your actual addresses before running

@BASE = http://localhost:3004
@NEW_WALLET  = 0x1122334455667788990011223344556677889900aabbccddeeff001122334455
@OLD_COL     = 0xdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
@NEW_COL     = 0xcafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafecafe

###
# STEP 0 — Health check
GET {{BASE}}/health HTTP/1.1

###
# STEP 1 — Get attester public key
# Copy x and y into your NFT contract constructor (migration_attester_pubkey_x/y)
GET {{BASE}}/attester HTTP/1.1

###
# STEP 2 — Mint a fresh migration secret (stateless; nothing is stored)
# Save `secret`. Pass old collection + `commitment` to register_migration() on the OLD rollup.
GET {{BASE}}/migration/new-secret HTTP/1.1

###
# STEP 2b — (optional) Recompute the commitment for a saved secret
POST {{BASE}}/migration/commitment HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "secret": "PASTE_SECRET_FROM_STEP_2_HERE"
}

###
# STEP 3 — Register collection mapping (collection owner, after deploying on new rollup)
POST {{BASE}}/collections/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "old_collection_address": "{{OLD_COL}}",
  "old_network": "testnet",
  "new_collection_address": "{{NEW_COL}}",
  "new_network": "testnet",
  "collection_name": "My NFT Collection"
}

###
# STEP 4 — Request signed migration data (Alice on NEW rollup)
# Reveal the `secret` from Step 2. The owner must already have called
# register_migration(commitment) on the old rollup and the indexer must have
# ingested it. Returns one signature per publicly-owned token.
POST {{BASE}}/request_data HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "collection_address": "{{NEW_COL}}",
  "migration_secret": "PASTE_SECRET_FROM_STEP_2_HERE",
  "new_wallet_address": "{{NEW_WALLET}}"
}

###
# STEP 5 — List registered collections
GET {{BASE}}/collections HTTP/1.1

###
# STEP 6 — Lookup a specific collection by new address
GET {{BASE}}/collections/{{NEW_COL}} HTTP/1.1
